course: dictionary
lesson: 15504
title: Subdivision: a smaller part of a whole
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A subdivision is a smaller part made when something that is already divided gets divided again. The word starts with «sub-», which often means smaller or under. Think of it as a small piece inside a bigger piece.
explain: On a ruler, each centimetre is subdivided into ten millimetres. «Each centimetre on the ruler is subdivided into ten millimetres.» The millimetres are the small marks inside each centimetre, so you must count them carefully.
explain: Subdivision can also mean the act of dividing something into smaller parts. «The teacher's subdivision of the class into four groups took only a minute.» Here it is the action, not the parts.
explain: In North America, Australia and New Zealand, a subdivision is an area of land split into plots where new houses are built. «They live in a new subdivision on the edge of town.» This is the same idea: a bigger piece of land cut into smaller pieces.
fact: A subdivision is a smaller part of something that has already been divided.
fact: The prefix «sub-» often means smaller or under, so a subdivision is a smaller piece inside a bigger one.
fact: «Subdivided» means divided again into smaller parts, as in «subdivided into millimetres».
fact: A county is a subdivision of a state or country, and it is one of its smaller areas.
fact: In the US, Canada, Australia and New Zealand, «subdivision» can mean a housing estate: land cut into plots for new houses.
exercise: «Each centimetre on the ruler is subdivided into ten millimetres.» What does subdivided mean here? | Joined together | *Divided into smaller parts | Measured in litres | Painted red
exercise: «The county is a subdivision of the state.» What is a subdivision here? | A bigger, whole area | *A smaller part of a bigger area | A kind of animal | A type of sweet
exercise: Mum says, «They live in a new subdivision» (Australia). What is a subdivision here? | A school for young children | A river crossing | A shop that sells bread | *An area of land divided into plots where new houses are built
test: The word «subdivision» starts with «sub-», which often means smaller or under. What does this suggest? | *Something smaller inside something bigger | Something made of wood | A very large, whole thing | A type of water
test: «The map showed each subdivision of the county in a different colour.» What are the subdivisions on this map? | Ocean waves | *Smaller parts of the county | Whole countries | Different kinds of paint
exam: The number line has marks for tenths, which are a subdivision of each whole number. What is a subdivision of a whole number? | A bigger number | A line drawn in ink | A negative number | *A smaller part of the whole number
